    "unit": 39,
    "title": "Countable/Uncountable Nouns (Advanced)",
    "title_ko": "가산·불가산 명사 심화",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Some nouns are always uncountable in English even though their translation is countable in other languages (advice, information, furniture, luggage). Use quantifiers like 'a piece of', 'a lot of', 'a bit of' instead of a plural -s: 'a piece of advice', not 'an advice'.",
    "explanation_ko": "일부 명사는 다른 언어에서는 셀 수 있어도 영어에서는 항상 셀 수 없습니다(advice, information, furniture, luggage). 복수형 -s 대신 'a piece of', 'a lot of', 'a bit of' 같은 수량 표현을 씁니다: 'a piece of advice'(O), 'an advice'(X).",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "Can I give you a piece of advice?",
        "ko": "조언 하나 드려도 될까요?"
      },
      {
        "en": "I need some information about the schedule.",
        "ko": "일정에 대한 정보가 좀 필요해요."
      },
      {
        "en": "We bought a lot of new furniture.",
        "ko": "우리는 새 가구를 많이 샀어요."
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
